✅ Q16 — Find the Longest String in a List

🎗️ 16.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<String> containing strings of different lengths.
Using Java Streams, find the longest string in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as an Optional<String> or handle the empty list appropriately.
🔴 Correctly handle strings with different lengths.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate strings.
🔴 Correctly handle empty strings.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Do not modify the original list.

🎗️ 16.2 Input / Output

👉 Input List

Use this exact list in your Java program:
List<String> words = Arrays.asList("Java","Spring","Microservices","API","Docker","Kubernetes","AWS");

👉 Expected Output
Microservices

Because:

Java          → 4 characters
Spring        → 6 characters
Microservices  → 12 characters  ✅
API           → 3 characters
Docker        → 6 characters
Kubernetes    → 10 characters
AWS           → 3 characters

🎗️ 16.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.
You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches — Streams only
🔴 How you handle an empty list
🔴 How you handle multiple strings having the same maximum length
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too.
